      "content": "Mounds and scuffling marks, especially at night, could indicate a few different things, and it's wise to keep an eye on it. While it could be beneficial soil life, those distinct mounds and scurry marks might suggest some surface-feeding pests, like tiny slugs, snails, or even certain types of beetles. These pests can sometimes feed on young kale tissue, which might exacerbate nutrient stress symptoms like yellowing. It's a good idea to inspect those mounds closely in the early morning to identify what is causing them.",
